#.view-directives.tsvt — what a viewport does with this grid, declared in the file itself.
#.header names the rows that label the data. freeze pins them, and the totals row at
#.the bottom, while the middle scrolls. hide keeps the scratch column out of sight
#.without taking it out of the sheet: `tsv render` still prints it, and only
#.`tsv render --hidden=drop` leaves it out. Delete all four #. lines and the numbers
#.are identical — a directive is a projection of the grid, never an input to it.
#.header	rows(count(1))
#.freeze	rows(count(1), count(-1))
#.hide	cols(range(D:D))
Region	Units	Revenue	Unit price (scratch)
North	120	=B2*D2	4.25
South	80	=B3*D3	4.25
East	95	=B4*D4	4.25
West	140	=B5*D5	4.25
Total	=sum(B2:B5)	=sum(C2:C5)	
